* PIP - CP/M FILE COPY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* PIP - CP/M FILE COPY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:PIP destination=source[,source...]

Copies files or device streams. The destination is on the LEFT of the
equals sign. Example: SYSUTLS:PIP I0:COPY.TXT=I0:SOURCE.TXT

Wildcards and options can affect many files. [V] requests write
verification; text/binary and device options need care. Check the
destination and free space first. PIP is private here; caller transfers
use UPLOAD or YSEND.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
